<title>UK: BASKETBALL-FINAL EUROLEAGUE GROUP STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-FINAL EUROLEAGUE GROUP STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Final men's EuroLeague basketball</p>
<p>group standings after Thursday's matches:</p>
<p>Group E</p>
<p> Stefanel Milan (Italy)	    16  11   5   27</p>
<p> Alba Berlin (Germany)	     16  10   6   26</p>
<p> Olympiakos (Greece)		 16   9   7   25</p>
<p> Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel)	 16   9   7   25</p>
<p> CSKA Moscow (Russia)		16   8   8   24</p>
<p> Charleroi (Belgium)		 16   1  15   17</p>
<p>Group F</p>
<p> Teamsystem Bologna (Italy)	16  12   4   28</p>
<p> Cibona Zagreb (Croatia)	   16  10   6   26</p>
<p> Estudiantes Madrid (Spain)	16   9   7   25</p>
<p> Limoges (France)		    16   8   8   24</p>
<p> Ulker Spor (Turkey)		 16   5  11   21</p>
<p> Panionios (Greece)		  16   4  12   20</p>
<p>Group G</p>
<p> Panathinaikos (Greece)	    16  13   3   29</p>
<p> Villeurbanne (France)	     16  12   4   28</p>
<p> Ljubljana (Slovenia)		16  10   6   26</p>
<p> Sevilla (Spain)		     16   7   9   23</p>
<p> Pau-Orthez (France)		 16   6  10   22</p>
<p> Dynamo Moscow (Russia)	    16   3  13   19</p>
<p>Group H</p>
<p> Efes Pilsen (Turkey)		16  12   4   28</p>
<p> Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia)  16   9   7   25</p>
<p> Barcelona (Spain)		   16   8   8   24</p>
<p> Kinder Bologna (Italy)	    16   7   9   23</p>
<p> Split (Croatia)		     16   7   9   23</p>
<p> Bayer Leverkusen (Germany)	16   2  14   18</p>
<p>Top four from each group now qualify for last 16 which is</p>
<p>played on a knock-out basis. Games to be played over two legs on</p>
<p>March 6 and 11 with third game on March 13 if necessary.</p>
</text>
